# One git branch per roadmap item

- Each catalog item (`F07-001`, `F07-008`, `F08-014`, …) is implemented, committed, and pushed on **its own branch**.
- Branch name: `feature/07_<id>_<short_slug>` (example: `feature/07_008_position_transformation`). Keep the numeric id from the plan.
- Do not mix another item’s code into that branch. Shared files may change only as needed for the current id.
- Start the branch from the last pushed item (or `main` if the plan says so). After the item is done, push that branch; do not fold the next item into it.
- P0 vs P1 only chooses **order**. It does not allow bundling several ids on one branch.
